      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In 1975 Bronx, the street-level inhabitants could be broken down into several categories: young couples with infants or toddlers, predominantly African American or Latino families and fathers, traditionally dressed in Afros, baggy clothing, and basketball jewelry; working-class brows and worn summer suits. You'll also see children playing in the park or riding bicycles, often with Crocs-style helmets and braids tied up in the back. Neighborhood businessmen and local vendors selling affordable street food and dry goods, while older neighbors adding charm with carefully kept across-the-street planters. These diverse groups add depth and textual coherence to your development of the naturalism for the film's authentic portrayal.",
